WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.600
Welcome to Grade 1 English, Unit 9: City Places.

2
00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:07.320
In this unit you will learn the words for places in a town.

3
00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:11.700
They are the shop, the market, the
school, the hospital and the library.

4
00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:14.980
You will learn about the people who work in these places.

5
00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:20.660
You will learn the words that tell us
where something is: near, far and next to.

6
00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:22.740
You will meet the traffic lights too.

7
00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:24.260
Red means stop.

8
00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:25.900
Green means go.

9
00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:29.420
A town is full of helpful places and kind people.

10
00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:32.380
We all help to keep it clean and safe.

11
00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:38.400
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

12
00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:46.560
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name places
in a town (shop, market, school, hospital, library, park).

13
00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:51.880
You will also name some people who
help us (teacher, doctor, shopkeeper).

14
00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:57.600
You will also say where a place is using
position words (near, next to, here, there).

15
00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:00.140
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

16
00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:06.180
Your vocabulary work begins with these
words: flag, swim, stop, step, drum, tent.

17
00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:11.780
Listen to each word, look at what it means,
and try to use it when you talk and write.

18
00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:17.320
The reading sequence includes A Walk
Around Town and Talk about City Places.

19
00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:23.220
Read slowly, look at the pictures,
and find the big idea in each text.

20
00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:26.800
When you answer a question, point to the words that show it.

21
00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:30.900
The first language focus is Say what is in your town.

22
00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:33.140
Name one place in your town.

23
00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:39.340
Say 'a' before most words, but 'an'
before a vowel sound: a shop, an airport.

24
00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:43.320
Look at the examples, then try
the pattern in your own sentences.

25
00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:48.840
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 - Listen and point.

26
00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:52.180
Say your ideas clearly and listen to your partner.

27
00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:58.940
In writing, you will draw, trace, copy or write,
then check your work with a grown-up or the AI tutor.

28
00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:00.600
You are ready to begin.

29
00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:06.800
Start with the words, then the reading and the
questions, then the grammar, speaking and writing.

30
00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:13.280
Ask the AI tutor for help any time, and bring your
questions to a live session too if you join one.
